#!/usr/local/bin/python3.13 -I
"""ai-releases: near-real-time alerts to the owner about new FRONTIER AI models (flagship-class general models
about such releases as soon as possible, after he once learned of a major model launch before I told him).

  ai-releases run [--dry-run] [--days N] [--no-judge] [-v]
        cron (every 15 min): fetch due sources -> keyword/heuristic filter -> local-LLM judge -> tg alert per release.
        --dry-run: nothing is sent or saved (judge results are cached). --days N (implies --dry-run): ignore the state
        and show what it would have flagged among everything dated within the last N days (pages: baseline only).
  ai-releases seed            fetch every source now and mark all of it as already known (no alerts)
  ai-releases status          sources (last ok, failures), queue, alerts sent today, recent alerts
  ai-releases known [add NAME | rm NAME]   names treated as already alerted (dedup across sources, 21 days)

Sources (no tokens in the cron path; fetching and robots.txt via ~/bin/watch's helpers, same polite UA):
  feeds   Google AI blog, Gemini blog, Google DeepMind blog, Google Developers blog, OpenAI news, Anthropic news (a
          community RSS mirror of anthropic.com/news; Anthropic has no feed), Mistral news, Claude Code releases
          (major versions only)
  hn      HN stories with >= 150 points (Algolia API), AI names + release words
  hf      Hugging Face: newest models of the big open-weight orgs (Qwen, deepseek-ai, meta-llama, mistralai, google,
          openai, moonshotai, zai-org, MiniMaxAI, xai-org, nvidia, microsoft), grouped into families, >= 100 likes;
          and HF trending (created < 21 days, >= 300 likes)
  pages   change detection on the labs' official model pages (Gemini, OpenAI models, Claude models overview, Mistral
          models, xAI models): new model names and availability lines (preview -> GA, new tiers, API) -> "🔄 Update".
          Meta's pages are skipped (Meta's terms forbid automated collection; ~/bin/watch refuses Meta too): Meta is
          covered by HN and HF meta-llama.
Pipeline: cheap regex filter (AI names + release words, minus funding/partners/customer stories/rumours), then a
deterministic exclusion stage (image/video/audio families, mini/nano/lite/small/distilled variants, product-feature
phrasing; allow list wins; config ~/.config/ai-releases/exclude.json, see DENY_NAME), then the LOCAL LLM
(`llm-local --system ... --json`, public data only) rates "major release?" and writes one line; alert only on yes
(the exclusion stage re-checks the judge's release name). Judge down (timeout, exit, bad JSON): fail closed, no alert,
the item stays a candidate for the next run. Dedup: every item id once; release names (judge's name or the name in
the title) 21 days across all sources.
Delivery: `tg` one short message per release; quiet hours 00:00-08:00 Zurich queue it until 08:00; at most
DAILY_CAP (6) per day, the overflow goes to one ~/inbox note. A new source's first fetch only seeds (no backlog flood).
State: ~/.local/state/ai-releases/ (state.json, judge-cache.json, log). Tests: ~/opt/ai-releases-tests/run.sh.
Env (tests): AI_RELEASES_STATE_DIR, AI_RELEASES_INBOX, AI_RELEASES_TG (sender), AI_RELEASES_NOW (epoch or
"YYYY-MM-DD HH:MM" Zurich), AI_RELEASES_JUDGE (judge command: reads the prompt on stdin, prints JSON),
AI_RELEASES_FIXTURES (dir: <source>.<ext> instead of HTTP), AI_RELEASES_SOURCES (comma list), AI_RELEASES_DAILY_CAP,
AI_RELEASES_EXCLUDE (exclusion config path), AI_RELEASES_JUDGE_TIMEOUT (seconds, default 240).
"""
